    "distractors": {
      "C": "Event-driven (Pub/Sub-triggered) functions are capped at a 540-second timeout even in 2nd gen, so a 45-minute job is terminated after 9 minutes; only HTTP functions reach 60 minutes.",
      "D": "A Spot VM can be preempted with 30 seconds' notice mid-backup and the fixed 02:00 stop truncates any run that overruns, with no retry, task tracking or completion status.",
      "B": "It still forces the batch code to wrap itself in an HTTP listener and hold one request open for 45 minutes; any client or proxy disconnect kills the run with no completion or retry semantics."
    },
