      "A": "One container means one PID 1: Cloud Run's startup and liveness probes and its per-container CPU/memory limits apply to the whole image, so a collector that dies inside the supervisor is invisible to the platform.",
      "B": "Separate services have independent lifecycles and autoscaling, so they are not in the same instance: the required localhost path and shared instance lifecycle become billable cross-service network round trips."
