    "correct": "C",
    "explanation": "Security Command Center (SCC) includes native Compliance Dashboards and the Security Posture Service with predefined regulatory benchmarks (HIPAA, PCI-DSS, CIS, ISO 27001), continuously mapping findings to regulatory requirements.",
    "distractors": {
      "D": "Audit logs record who invoked which API and when, which is activity rather than posture: a bucket that has been public since creation generates no audit event, so the dashboard cannot report the misconfigurations the Compliance Officer is required to attest to.",
      "A": "Cloud Asset Inventory returns resource configuration snapshots, not security findings, so every misconfiguration detection, every control mapping and every scoring rule has to be written and then maintained by hand as the HIPAA benchmark and Google's resource schemas change.",
      "B": "Assured Workloads is preventive: it constrains data residency, support personnel access and which services may be provisioned in the folder. It never evaluates the posture of resources already deployed, so unencrypted disks and public buckets produce no finding and no score."
    },
